==Enemy==
The boss of the first Chapter's final stage, The Face has extremely high health and attack but is the slowest enemy in the game. Additionally, he attacks very infrequently, rendering his highly devastating attacks useless in the presence of meatshields and 350+ range cats.

Later on in the game, this enemy becomes more defensively-focused, as his 1 speed keeps him from straying too far away from the enemy base, along with late-game buffs making his high health and high attack power skyrocket to where he can destroy most of your units with a single chomp.

==Strategy==
Use long-ranged units such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]] and/or [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] to hit him from a distance, while dealing constant damage.

It is recommended to only use [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] that can outrange him, but even then, because of his 1 movement speed, there is not much reason to use any effect other than [[Weaken]] or [[Freeze]]. [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] that work especially well against The Face include, but are not limited to: [[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]], [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]], [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]], [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|Megidora]], [[M. Bison (Uber Rare Cat)|M. Bison]], [[Madoka Kaname (Uber Rare Cat)|Madoka Kaname]], [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Shining Amaterasu]], [[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman]], and virtually any other generalist or [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] Uber.

You can also take advantage of his long interval between attacks by using units such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Express Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]] and/or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], to get some quick damage off. Otherwise, he should not be the main focus for your lineup in many of the stages he appears in.

