==Trivia==
*His real name is "Kaoru Hikao" or "Kaoru Higao" (飛顔かおる), as shown at the bottom of the screen with other enemy names in a [https://youtu.be/GZRyiPUY7dA commercial] for the [[Final Boss Strikes?! Collaboration Event]]. Hikao/Higao is not an actual surname that anyone has in real life, but a pun using the kanji for "fly" (飛) and "face" (顔). Kaoru is a real name, but is also being used as a pun: ''kao'' means "face".
*His appearance is a close match for the profile of [[wikipedia:Masaoka Shiki|Masaoka Shiki]], a poet and essayist in Meiji period Japan, albeit without any facial hair.
*He may take inspiration from [https://yokai.com/ookubi/ Ōkubi], a floating head ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' whose name literally means "giant head".
*[[Pumpcat (Rare Cat)|Harbinger Cat]] attacks by dropping smaller Faces down on enemies. This may be a reference to [https://yokai.com/tsurubeotoshi/ tsurube otoshi], a giant head ''yōkai'' that drops down on its prey from treetops.
**The flaming [[Shy Boy]] variant from [[Nyanko Defence Force]] may have also been inspired by tsurube otoshi, since it descended from the top of the screen and tsurube otoshi are said to sometimes appear wreathed in flames like large fireballs.
*The stone bust of The Face in Nyanko Defence Force may have been a visual pun on a [[wikipedia:Rock face|rock face]] or the term ''stone-faced''.
*[[I.M. Phace]]'s Japanese description suggests that the smaller Phace inside his mouth is actually The Face himself, somehow shrunken down and using the larger Phace as a mobile villa.
*In [[Teacher Cybear]]'s Japanese description, it's stated that he freeloaded at The Face's house for 6 years without going outside.
*The Face is the first [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy in terms of ID, but not the first encountered in-game - that honor goes to [[Mooth]], who has a higher ID than The Face despite appearing earlier.
*He has a higher ID than Shy Boy and [[Assassin Bear]] despite appearing earlier.
*The Face, [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[Teacher Bun Bun]] all share the same amount of health: 99,999. However, Nyandam only has [[Soul Leasing|one unbuffed appearance]], and Teacher Bun Bun has so far always been fought at 400% or more.
*[[Sage of Mind Soractes]] can be seen as a foil to The Face:
**Both are mid-ranged Floating enemies that are predominantly white.
**The Face's diet caused him to lose everything but his face, whereas Soractes has a full body but lacks a face.
**The Face is extremely slow in both movement speed and attack rate, whereas Soractes moves quickly and attacks non-stop.
**Both are bosses of the 48th stages of Japan. The [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]] of [[Empire of Cats]] takes place across the 47 prefectures of Japan and [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] rather than various countries and the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]], while [[Adherence to Virtue]] is the 48th and last [[Zero Legends]] stage to take place in a [[Media:Map040.png|jumbled up and mirrored Japan]].
**Adherence to Virtue's [https://youtu.be/_KhgY0ArzW4 theme] contains the leitmotif of "[https://youtu.be/5yyyqU-Y7lA Lunar Battle]", which first plays against The Face.
**Both are the first major bosses of their respective areas (if one does not count [[Metafilibuster (Enemy)|Metafilibuster]] as the first major boss of Zero Legends).
*He is tied with [[Mega Cat EX (Enemy)|Mega Cat EX]] for being the slowest non-stationary enemy in the game.
*[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] is the only standard enemy type without a variant of The Face.
*One of [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' later games, ''Heads Off'', may be based entirely off of The Face, since it features floating heads that open their mouths wide. He even makes an appearance in it as one of the unlockable characters.
*From [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] to [[Version 5.9 Update|Version 5.9]], The Face was a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/Floating enemy.

